.Dd August 31, 2026
.Dt HAWKEYE 8
.Os CloudBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm hawkeye
.Nd FreeBSD diagnostic and operations doctor (MASH)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar query ...
.Nm
.Op Fl -config Ar path
.Op Fl -check-config
.Op Fl -json
.Ar command
.Op Ar args
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a privileged FreeBSD diagnostic and operations tool.
It consults a local knowledge corpus (from the sibling
.Nm hawkeye-data
project), optionally a local or remote LLM, and can apply operator-confirmed
plans.
It is
.Em not
a public chat UI.
.Pp
With no command, on a terminal,
.Nm
is the panic path: a short
.Ql hawkeye
banner, a host first-look
.Pq human text, not JSON ,
then a
.Ql >
prompt.
The first-look inspects the
.Em host
immediately: root read-only versus read-write and filesystem type, missing
.Pa /usr ,
.Pa /etc/fstab
versus mounts, zpool health, rc
.Li *_enable
versus missing scripts or binaries
.Pq rc.d command= expands ${name} and $name from the script basename like rc.subr; inspect does not start services ,
network carrier and default route,
disk and inode headroom, and geli keystatus.
Each line is one actionable finding.
Silence means that subsystem looks fine.
This is not
.Nm doctor
.Pq Hawkeye service self-health: config, pidfile, knowledge .
Type the problem
.Pq one line .
Each line is a consult, then
.Dq Apply these steps? [y/N/e]
as for
.Nm consult .
Empty lines re-prompt.
.Cm quit ,
.Cm exit ,
.Cm q ,
and EOF leave with status 0.
.Cm help
and
.Ql ?
print a short reminder.
Positional words that are not a known command are the first query;
on a TTY the session continues.
Without a terminal and with no arguments, print a short reminder to run
.Nm
on a terminal
.Pq do not wait on a pipe .
.Fl -json
with no command dumps host first-look JSON and never enters the session.
.Pp
Knowledge is consumed, never vendored in this repository.
.Sh INSTALLATION
Install the binary and knowledge kit together:
.Pp
.Dl pkg install hawkeye
.Pp
.Nm
depends on
.Nm hawkeye-data
and pulls the corpus in.
A second
.Nm pkg
install of the data port is not required.
.Pp
Rescue layout
.Pq static-capable binary and RO knowledge prefix :
.Pp
.Dl make install-rescue
.Pp
That stages
.Pa /rescue/hawkeye
and creates
.Pa /boot/hawkeye
under
.Ev DESTDIR
.Pq the build chroot need not have a live
.Pa /boot
or
.Pa /rescue
.Ns .
Override
.Ev RESCUE_DIR
and
.Ev BOOT_HAWKEYE
if those prefixes differ.
The knowledge sqlite and playbooks come from
.Nm hawkeye-data
.Pq dual prefix
and are not vendored here.
Set
.Ev KNOWLEDGE_SRC
to copy a sqlite file into the rescue kit.
On a live host,
.Pa /rescue
is written only when it is a real directory.
A dangling bastille
.Pa /rescue
symlink
.Pq thin jail
is skipped.
.Pa /boot/hawkeye
is created when
.Pa /boot
exists.
The port option
.Cm RESCUE
is off by default and stages the same paths under
.Ev DESTDIR
.Ns .
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Nm
With no command, start the panic-path operator session on a terminal.
This is the intended invocation when the host is on fire.
The session starts with host first-look, then
.Ql > .
.It Nm inspect
Host first-look only
.Pq the same findings as the session banner .
Diagnose only; no mutation.
Default stdout is human text.
.Fl -json
or
.Ev HAWKEYE_JSON
emits the structured findings object.
Does not enter the session.
Not
.Nm doctor .
.It Nm consult Op Ar query
Diagnose using FTS knowledge and an optional LLM.
Default stdout is an operator session: the most actionable playbook for
the query
.Pq title, stored summary, stored commands ,
then related titles.
When a local model runs, the completion is printed after the playbook
hits.
It does not print query or tier keys, ranks, or an
.Dq llm skipped
line
.Pq no model is a quiet TTY skip;
.Fl -json
may still note it
.Ns .
.Fl -json
or
.Ev HAWKEYE_JSON
set to
.Li 1
emits the machine object instead.
On a TTY
.Pq stdin is a terminal
and without
.Fl -json ,
after the recommendation prompt
.Dq Apply these steps? [y/N/e] .
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
.Cm y / yes
turns the recommendation into a plan and dry-runs it unless
.Fl -yes
was already given.
After a dry-run, ask
.Dq Apply for real? [y/N]
which is the same gate as
.Nm apply Fl -yes .
Enter, empty, and EOF default to
.Cm N
and do not mutate.
.It
.Cm e / edit
writes the plan JSON to a temp file, opens
.Ev VISUAL ,
then
.Ev EDITOR ,
then
.Ic vi ,
re-reads the file
.Pq JSON plan or a command list
and uses the same apply confirm.
An aborted or empty editor does not apply.
.It
.Cm n
or EOF prints
.Dq nothing applied
and exits 0.
.El
Invalid keys re-prompt.
Non-TTY,
.Fl -json ,
.Ev HAWKEYE_JSON ,
and MCP consult never prompt.
Scripts keep
.Nm consult
then
.Nm plan
then
.Nm apply Fl -dry-run
or
.Nm apply Fl -yes .
On a read-only root the first skill is
.Cm unlock-rw ,
not
.Cm pkg .
.It Nm plan Op Ar query
Propose steps from the lead consult playbook
.Pq stored
.Cm commands
JSON or fenced body lines
.Ns .
It does not invent
.Ic echo
.Ar query
stubs.
No mutation.
Default stdout is operator-readable prose.
.Fl -json
or
.Ev HAWKEYE_JSON
emits the JSON plan for
.Nm apply .
Apply still defaults to dry-run;
.Fl -yes
is required to land.
.It Nm apply Op Fl -dry-run | Fl -yes Op Ar plan.json
Apply a plan.
The default is dry-run.
.Fl -yes
is required to mutate.
LLM actors never execute privileged steps; the operator CLI is the mutator.
Playbook command lists run in one
.Pa /bin/sh
session so assignments such as
.Li ROOTDS=
persist into later
.Li zfs set \&"$ROOTDS\&"
steps.
A failed step does not report applied and exits non-zero.
Plan JSON is parsed first; secrets are redacted per field, not against the raw document.
Applies are audited.
If the audit log directory cannot be created
.Pq read-only root, missing
.Pa /var
.Ns ,
apply still lands and notes the skip on stderr.
.It Nm doctor
Service health: configuration, permissions, pidfile, dependencies, and
resource headroom.
Prints human-readable evidence and JSON.
Exits non-zero if unhealthy.
.It Nm mcp Op Fl -stdio | Fl -http
MCP server.
.Fl -stdio
is the default and does not require a token.
.Fl -http
is Streamable HTTP bound to loopback
.Pq 127.0.0.1
by default.
HTTP requires a bearer token from
.Ev HAWKEYE_MCP_TOKEN
or the environment variable named by
.Va listen.mcp_token_env .
nginx terminates TLS and reverse-proxies
.Pa /mcp
to the loopback listener.
Public URL:
.Lk https://hawkeye.revytechinc.com/mcp .
GET is Server-Sent Events after authentication; POST is JSON-RPC.
Missing or wrong token returns HTTP 401.
The token is never written to logs or documentation.
MCP tools use the same plan/apply gate as the operator CLI:
the same executor and audit log.
Unprivileged
.Cm apply
still requires
.Cm yes
.Pq the
.Fl -yes
gate
.Ns .
Privileged MCP apply stays dry-run even when
.Cm yes
is set.
.It Nm update
Refresh knowledge artifacts from
.Nm hawkeye-data
when the root is writable.
Destination defaults to
.Pa /usr/local/share/hawkeye/knowledge.sqlite
.Pq the system knowledge path already in use
.Ns .
Source is
.Fl -src ,
.Va update.source ,
or
.Ev HAWKEYE_UPDATE_SOURCE
.Pq
.Ev HAWKEYE_DATA_ARTIFACT
is a legacy alias
.Ns .
If the source is unset, the command skips with status 0 so
.Xr rc 8
start stays healthy.
A set source on a read-only root is still refused
.Pq first skill is
.Cm unlock-rw
.Ns .
.It Nm init Op Ar dir
Write a sample JSON configuration
.Pq mode 0600 .
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl -config Ar path
JSON configuration file.
Default search:
.Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/hawkeye/config.json
if present, else
.Pa /usr/local/etc/cloudbsd/hawkeye/config.json .
The live file is optional; a missing file uses compiled defaults.
.It Fl -check-config
Validate the configuration and exit.
A missing file is valid and uses compiled defaults
.Pq the same as
.Nm doctor
.Ns .
A present file is parsed as RFC 8259 JSON and validated.
Invalid JSON fails.
Must succeed before a SIGHUP reload.
.It Fl -json
Prefer JSON output for
.Nm consult ,
.Nm plan ,
.Nm inspect ,
and
.Nm doctor .
With no command, dump host first-look JSON and do not enter the session.
Consult does not prompt.
Never starts the panic-path operator session.
.It Fl -dry-run
Force apply dry-run
.Pq default .
Wins over
.Fl -yes
on
.Nm apply
and on a TTY consult confirm.
.It Fl -yes
Permit mutation for
.Nm apply .
On a TTY
.Nm consult ,
skips the second
.Dq Apply for real?
prompt after the operator answers
.Cm y
or finishes an edit.
The first prompt still defaults to
.Cm N .
.El
.Sh SIGNALS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Dv SIGHUP
Validate the configuration
.Pq same rules as Fl -check-config
then reload in place.
If validation fails, keep the old process and old configuration.
Reload is a no-op failure, not a crash.
.El
.Sh TIERS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It 0
Rescue: read-only root, maybe no
.Pa /usr
or
.Pa /var ,
no network, no GPU.
Knowledge from
.Pa /boot/hawkeye .
FTS only; LLM not required.
.It 1
Root writable, islanded.
CPU embedder if RAM allows.
.It 2
Network up.
Carrier is a non-loopback interface from getifaddrs,
.Dv SIOCGIFMEDIA ,
or
.Nm ifconfig
.Dq status: active .
Linux
.Pa /sys/class/net
is not the FreeBSD probe.
May escalate large jobs to a remote LLM.
GPU is used if it works and is not required otherwise.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/cloudbsd/hawkeye/config.json
System configuration
.Pq optional; missing uses compiled defaults .
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/cloudbsd/hawkeye/config.json.sample
Installed sample
.Pq mode 0644; no secrets .
Not loaded unless copied to
.Pa config.json .
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/rc.d/hawkeye
rc.d script.
.It Pa /var/run/hawkeye.pid
Pidfile
.Pq mode 0644 ; the PID is not a secret .
.It Pa /rescue/hawkeye
Static-capable rescue binary
.Pq
.Nm make install-rescue
or port option
.Cm RESCUE
.Ns .
.It Pa /boot/hawkeye
Rescue knowledge prefix
.Pq read-only kit; dual prefix with
.Pa /usr/local/share/hawkeye
.Ns .
.It Pa /boot/hawkeye/knowledge.sqlite
Rescue
.Pa knowledge.sqlite
and playbooks from
.Nm hawkeye-data
.Pq not vendored in this repository .
.It Pa /usr/local/share/hawkeye
System knowledge artifacts from
.Nm hawkeye-data .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Nm doctor
exits non-zero when unhealthy.
